{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as an implementation plan at exact head 087da4407e087e451574e7d734a2361d660ebf39, covering the sole artifact notes/2026-10-01-artroom-plan.md.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: approved. The Room remains the authoritative sequencer; proposed heads and generations are immutable. Landing is authorized by a synchronous durable reservation, with parallel preparation and one publication slot. Retrying the same reserved integration resolves uncertain ordinary pushes forward without permitting a second reservation. Failed/uncertain publication remains visible and holds the slot. Token expiry is explicitly not treated as proof of remote cancellation. Published-prefix verification and publication lag have honest limits.\n\nSecurity conclusion: approved at plan level. New acts use verified canonical envelopes and current admission authority. Earlier evidence uses recorded admission authority plus explicit current validity rules, preserving retired-key and expired-delegation evidence while invalidating compromise evidence before reservation. Post-reservation compromise is a recorded best-effort abort, with landed/revert, aborted only on terminal proof, or unresolved outcomes. Runner isolation, whole-tree check inputs by default, scoped snapshots with actual confinement, volatile-input restrictions, pinned evaluation budgets, policy administration and pre-publication secret detection have defined boundaries.\n\nSimplification conclusion: approved. The complete functional scope remains the objective, as directed by hugh and recorded in asserts 19a32703 and f92ef928. Staging and the deployed vertical slice organize work; estimates and staffing suggestions do not constrain functionality. One typed vocabulary, explicit refusal/failure distinction, operation states and bounded cursors provide a coherent basis for the clients and UI.\n\nResolution of prior findings:\n- Review c31169e9: approval reuse is explicit and limited; checks bind their inputs and environment; safe publication and recovery are specified; authorization and actual changed-path requirements are explicit; immutable-secret limitations are acknowledged; API transitions and evidence qualifications are present.\n- Review 8233c002: publication has a defined reservation order; checks use complete inputs by default; revocation is determined at sequenced admission.\n- Review bce3646e: no publication slot is released merely on expiry or sandbox termination; reservation validates the initiator's current authority separately from historical evidence; emergency compromise outcomes are consistent. The runner example is now labeled as an Artroom wrapper and checks installation failure.\n\nImplementation reviews will validate the promised acceptance cases, especially delayed authenticated pushes, duplicate recovery attempts, restart between Git publication and receipt, negative review/release/revocation ordering, actual runner confinement, and deterministic evaluator failures. These are existing plan requirements, not added scope or conditions demanding code before the plan can land.\n\nRemaining choices, such as domain and npm scope, can be resolved during progress. Performance targets and platform processing bounds remain unmeasured. The Sandbox Git and Room-core spikes should report their evidence under their existing requests. This approval authorizes the plan artifact; it does not certify unbuilt runtime behavior or deployed security.\n\nValidation: read revision 2 in full and reviewed every change through exact revisions 3 and 4, together with the original request, artifact lineage, review reports, scope direction and relevant primary platform/Git documentation. The revised estimate totals 32 engineer-days; it is descriptive. Documentation review only: no application tests, deployment or source changes were performed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:149a6a3eae86c70c8589563ad2fa51e9a861f606","binding":"assigned